# Monitor build tree cleanup after verify

When you run **monitor Autotools** compile or test commands in a **configured build directory** under `HPCPerfStats/monitor` (canonical: **`HPCPerfStats/monitor/.build-static`**), run **`make distclean`** in **that same build directory** after verification succeeds.

## Ordering (do not break multi-step verify)

- If you run **more than one** compile/test step in the **same** build tree in one session (e.g. **`build_static_bundle.sh`** then **`make check`** in `.build-static`), run **`make distclean` only once**, **after the last** successful step—not between them.
- If verification **fails**, fix the failure first; run **`make distclean`** only after a **successful** final compile or test run for that pass.

## Scope

- Applies to **`make`**, **`make check`**, and other **compile/test** targets run in an Autotools **out-of-tree** build dir under **`HPCPerfStats/monitor/`**.
- Do **not** run **`make distclean`** in the **source** tree unless it is also the configured build directory (unusual for this project).
- **`PREFIX`** / **`.build/prefix-static`** from the static bundle scripts are separate from the Autotools build tree; this rule is about the directory that contains the generated **`Makefile`** (e.g. **`.build-static`**).

## Handoffs

When reporting verification, note that **`make distclean`** was run in the build tree after success (or state explicitly if you skipped cleanup because verification did not complete successfully).
